{"name":"Inuit Blue","hex":"#d8e4e7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Inuit","blocks":[{"text":"Inuit are a group of culturally and historically similar Indigenous peoples traditionally inhabiting the Arctic and Subarctic regions of North America and Russia, including Greenland, Labrador, Quebec, Nunavut, the Northwest Territories, Yukon (traditionally), and Alaska. The Inuit languages are part of the Eskaleut languages, also known as Inuit-Yupik-Unangan and as Eskimo–Aleut."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Distribution_of_Inuit_in_Canada_%282021%29.svg/330px-Distribution_of_Inuit_in_Canada_%282021%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inuit","wikidata":"Q189975"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Histoire_de_l%27Amerique_Septentrionale_-_divis%C3%A9e_en_quatre_tomes_%281753%29_%2814577039230%29.jpg/500px-Histoire_de_l%27Amerique_Septentrionale_-_divis%C3%A9e_en_quatre_tomes_%281753%29_%2814577039230%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Histoire_de_l%27Amerique_Septentrionale_-_divis%C3%A9e_en_quatre_tomes_%281753%29_%2814577039230%29.jpg/1280px-Histoire_de_l%27Amerique_Septentrionale_-_divis%C3%A9e_en_quatre_tomes_%281753%29_%2814577039230%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Histoire_de_l%27Amerique_Septentrionale_-_divis%C3%A9e_en_quatre_tomes_%281753%29_%2814577039230%29.jpg/500px-Histoire_de_l%27Amerique_Septentrionale_-_divis%C3%A9e_en_quatre_tomes_%281753%29_%2814577039230%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A European ship coming into contact with Inuit in the ice of Hudson Bay in 1697","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHistoire_de_l'Amerique_Septentrionale_-_divis%C3%A9e_en_quatre_tomes_(1753)_(14577039230).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Zentralbibliothek_Z%C3%BCrich_-_Merckliche_Beschreibung_sampt_eygenlicher_Abbildung_eynes_frembden_unbekanten_Volcks_-_000003625_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Zentralbibliothek_Z%C3%BCrich_-_Merckliche_Beschreibung_sampt_eygenlicher_Abbildung_eynes_frembden_unbekanten_Volcks_-_000003625_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Zentralbibliot